---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import AskBox from "../components/AskBox.astro";
import { asOf, manifest } from "../lib/data";
import { asOfLabel } from "../lib/format";

const cpiAsOf = asOf(["cpi_national.json"]);
const m = manifest();
---
<Base
  title="Ask the data — Malaysia Cost-of-Living Reality Check"
  description="Ask questions about Malaysian consumer prices, wages and household income. Answers are retrieved from the same data the charts use, with sources, or declined."
>
  <h1>Ask the data</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    A small agent that answers questions by looking figures up in the same dataset the charts
    are built from. It cannot answer from memory, and it will tell you when it does not know.
  </p>

  <AskBox />

  <h2>What it can and cannot do</h2>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card">
      <h3 style="margin-top:0">It can</h3>
      <ul class="plain">
        <li>Report inflation for any category, nationally or by state</li>
        <li>Rank the 16 states by inflation or real income growth</li>
        <li>Work out a personalised inflation rate from your spending split</li>
        <li>Show the 12-month CPI forecast, including where it fails</li>
        <li>Find what a specific grocery item costs in each state</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3 style="margin-top:0">It cannot</h3>
      <ul class="plain">
        <li>Answer anything about another country</li>
        <li>Say why something happened — this data shows what, not why</li>
        <li>Go beyond the forecast horizon, or before 2010 for states</li>
        <li>Give investment, legal or policy advice</li>
        <li>Recall a figure it did not just look up</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>How it is kept honest</h2>
  <p>
    Three things make this more than a chatbot with a dataset attached:
  </p>
  <ul class="plain">
    <li>
      <strong>It cannot answer without retrieving.</strong> If the model produces an answer
      without calling a single data tool, the answer is thrown away and replaced with a
      refusal. A remembered number and an invented number are indistinguishable, and both are
      unacceptable here, so the system makes the first impossible rather than merely discouraged.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Every figure carries its source.</strong> The tool results themselves carry the
      citation — dataset, date range, and the date that data was published — so the source is
      not something the model has to remember to mention.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Tool arguments are validated before execution.</strong> The model proposes, a
      schema disposes. A call naming a state that does not exist is rejected with the list of
      real ones, and a call naming a period outside the data is rejected rather than quietly
      answering about a different period.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <div class="callout warn">
    <h3>This runs on a free tier</h3>
    <p>
      The model runs on Cloudflare Workers AI, which allows 10,000 neurons per day at no cost.
      Questions are limited to 500 characters, rate limited per address, and each question may
      make at most six data lookups. If the box stops responding, that is the daily allowance
      rather than a fault. The charts, the calculator and every other page are static files and
      keep working regardless.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="callout">
    <h3>Prompt injection</h3>
    <p>
      Anything inside a tool result is treated as data, never as an instruction. Item names and
      any other text coming from the dataset are wrapped in explicit delimiters and the model is
      told that content within them cannot change its task. The answer is rendered as plain
      text, so nothing it returns can execute or restyle the page.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="data-note">
    <p>
      The agent reads the same artifacts this site does, built {m.generated_at.slice(0, 10)} by
      pipeline <code>v{m.pipeline_version}</code>. CPI as of {asOfLabel(cpiAsOf)}.
    </p>
    <p>
      Answers are generated text and can be wrong even with the guardrails above. The
      <a href="/methodology">methodology page</a> describes the underlying figures, which are
      what you should cite.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
